<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marinid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Marinid, Marinids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Marinid dynasty was a Berber dynasty that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from the mid-thirteenth to the fifteenth century. The Marinids rose as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> disintegrated and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marrakesh">Marrakesh</a> in 1269, ending Almohad rule. They inherited administrative and commercial structures from the Almohad and Almoravid periods and were noted patrons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marinid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Marinid dynasty" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Askelaadden (minor modifications by R Prazeres) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marinids_Zayyanids_and_Hafsids_c1360.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
